,"text":"). There are not that many such primes: each divisor "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" of number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" can correspond no more than one such prime, namely, the one whose power the number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 is (if it is a prime power at all). Let's calculate the set "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"P"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and also remember for each prime number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in it in which powers "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" the value ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1) divides "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we can calculate value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] that is equal to the number of ways to get a divisor "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" as a product of brackets of first "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" primes in set "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"P"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Such value can be caluclated by using dynamic programming in time "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/b3bc4a11e1ad2b54531b13649ee450298338ec74c957f889a05272ee6adc3e9a.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" where "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5dac71897c69036e72ae7069d3570ffcdc6bbc98ec9edbbb7e2f363211f16b5a.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the number of divisors of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (as it was shown above that "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/8c8e41e8fbd7b47022cc11fc65b2b00eba3bdeda18d0ba9e47f5521de4e8c3e2.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"). So, overall complexity of the solution is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/63fae1dd866cc0555127cfa35eb639ff80ced0dc032c7753f3b677a233d12f85.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Challenge"}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":". How the "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5dac71897c69036e72ae7069d3570ffcdc6bbc98ec9edbbb7e2f363211f16b5a.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" behaves when "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" increases? What is the maximum values of "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5dac71897c69036e72ae7069d3570ffcdc6bbc98ec9edbbb7e2f363211f16b5a.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" over all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"12"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"? (The answer: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/30d6fc2178dfba6eb30c12268812fe8ffa12f4078eb6fde1ce9a98e49941e2a8.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Nice estimate that is not an exact asymptotic, though, is that "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/aa9930976a6722a01a44dcc89ab13dfd1b190285fe92063920df546f000480cb.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Challenge"}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":". What is the maximum answer in this task? If you are able to create a test with answer larger than million, a great respect from me!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/542/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"542E - Playing on Graph"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First, if the original graph isn't bipartite then the answer is (-1). Indeed, any odd cycle, while being contracted by the pair of vertices, always produces an odd cycle of smaller size, so at some point we will get a triangle that blocks us from doing anything."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"From the other way, each bipartite component can be contracted in order to get a chain whose length is a diameter of the component. Suppose that the pair of vertices ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") is a diamater of some connected component. Then, by contracting all vertices located on the same distance from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we can achieve the chain we want."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The last step is that the answer fror the original graph is the sum of the answers for all the connected components since we can attach all of them together. So, the answer is the sum of diameters of all connected components if all of them are bipartite, otherwise answer is -1. Solution has the complexity "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"VE"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") (The first summand is checking for being bipartite, the second one is calculation diameters by running BFS from each vertex)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/542/problem/F"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"542F - Quest"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This task can be solved in lot of ways. The most straightforward is DP. The task can be seen in the following way. We want some set of vertices as leaves and for each potential leaf we know the upper bound for its depth and its cost."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's sweep over the tree from down to up. Let's calculate the value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] that is the maximum possible cost that we can achieve if we stay on the level "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and have "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices on it. For transition let's fix how many leaves of the deepness exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we will take (it's easy to see that among them we should task several greatest). Suppose we will take "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" of them. Then from this state we can move to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1][⌈("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") / 2⌉]. The answer will be located in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[0][1] because when we are on the level 0 we should have the only vertex that is the root of the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The complexity of such solution is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Challenge"}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" Improve the solution above to "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/919498b713ce08ee8d0e0dc67f34e966c65276354c614f78844a5dca89a03961.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" and then to "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/6c20aa71dda43f1457e2850b75957c3c5a9ef8b3316d5b28ef7ca21d8e22e8b4.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/17697"}